name: Claims
tagline: "A seeded insurance-claims Link Analysis demo - a staged-accident ring behind one garage, one clinic and one lawyer, planted among 380 claimants and 520 claims, with benign look-alikes"
description: "The insurance (Special Investigations Unit) Link Analysis demo as a Space Template: a Basic tier with an Advanced tier on top. Seven synthetic feeds (claim, claim_party, policy, provider_bill, accident_location, provider_directory, repair_invoice; one extract each in data/inbox, 18 months of claims, about 380 claimants, 25 providers, 520 claims) are landed by seven Collectors and Pipelines. The claims_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via) of nine link kinds; claims_policy_timing joins claims to policies. Planted stories (ground truth pinned by LaClaimsGoldenTest; tools/gen-la-claims-data.py): 12 claimants over 9 claims share 4 phones and 3 addresses and use one garage, one clinic and one lawyer; one of them is a passenger on 6 claims with 6 different drivers; 11 accidents at 02:00-04:00 within 400 m of one junction, none with a police report; the ring's clinic bills about 3x its peers and is referred to only by the ring's lawyer; 7 policies claimed on within 20 days of inception, all via one broker; two claimant records that are one person (resolvable by identity resolution); and benign look-alikes (a family of four sharing a phone and address, a busy general-practice clinic) that must not join the ring; a parts supplier invoicing 30 claims across all nine garages with no part fitted (look-alike: a larger supplier whose parts are all fitted); and a ghost broker whose 25 policies sit at addresses that do not exist and are paid from two bank accounts (look-alike: a family paying its four policies from one account). BASIC TIER (every edition, Basic included): the seven feeds, both Jobs, the five saved views, la_index_build (after claims_links is produced) and link-analysis.toon (one Entity Type party marked masked, the link index ON); masking_mode is left to the edition, so a Basic build, where nobody signs in, shows every id. The three saved Geo Views need the Geo map (Standard and above). ADVANCED TIER (a sign-in build; inert on Basic): typed masking of party ids with the admin's audited Reveal, the four-eyes fan-out threshold, Drafts limits and embed origins (link-analysis.toon), la_detect (every 5 minutes; with no Alert Rule bound it evaluates nothing), Demo Users and roles (roles.toon, demo-users.toon: siu.analyst lead, siu.manager second approver, partner.reviewer read-only, outsider not a member, admin reveal), and the runtime state the seed script writes (`node tools/seed-la-claims.mjs --apply`: Investigations, members, Entity Lists, identity groups, external references, a Case); the 12-minute walk-through is docs/okf/product/solution-pack/la-claims/admin-guide-showcase-runbook.md and needs an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth (serve-demo). Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:shield-check
contents[9]: "7 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (one extract each)", "claims_links Job + Dataset (9 link kinds, event_date, via)", "claims_policy_timing Job + Dataset", "link-analysis.toon (party Entity Type, index ON; typed masking, four-eyes and Drafts on sign-in builds)", "la_index_build Job (on claims_links produced)", "la_detect Job (cron; Advanced tier, evaluates nothing on Basic)", "5 saved views", "3 saved Geo Views (Standard and above) + 2 virtual accident Datasets", "5 Demo Users + role table (Advanced tier, inert on Basic)"
